   {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 🔧 IMPROVED SOLVER - Single LLM with Enhanced Debugging\n",
        "\n",
        "The analysis above shows the original two-LLM system has major issues:\n",
        "- Parser LLM generates incorrect \"short solutions\"\n",
        "- WizardMath solver itself is giving wrong answers\n",
        "- One test case has wrong expected answer (Problem 4: should be 50, not 60)\n",
        "\n",
        "Below is an improved single-LLM solver that addresses these issues:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "improved_solver_title"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# =========================\n",
        "# IMPROVED SINGLE-LLM SOLVER\n",
        "# =========================\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"🚀 LOADING IMPROVED SOLVER...\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Enhanced solver with better prompting\n",
        "def solve_with_improved_wizard(question: str, debug: bool = True) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Improved solver with better prompting and debugging\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    # Better system prompt following WizardMath best practices\n",
        "    improved_prompt = (\n",
        "        \"You are WizardMath, an expert in linear algebra and matrix operations.\\n\"\n",
        "        \"Solve determinant problems step by step with clear calculations.\\n\"\n",
